# THE DEFECT, on one line per run.
#
# SDPLIB truss6.dat-s at DEFAULT SETTINGS -- no environment variables of any kind. It routes
# sparse under the released `auto` policy (gate 4) and its 10,902 constraint pairs clear the
# 8,000-pair assembly gate, so the threaded assembly runs. Its 151 blocks share Schur-complement
# entries, so under the released `nowait` two workers in adjacent blocks could accumulate into
# the same dd_real.
#
# HOST: CANONICAL111, Apple M1 Max, 10 cores, aarch64, macOS. Thread count NOT varied and NOT
#       pinned: that is the point. Every row above is the same binary, same input, same
#       environment, same machine.
# BUILDS: "v7.1.3-omp.2" is the released tree rebuilt locally from the tag; "fixed" is dev with
#       the conditional barrier.
#
# The correct objective is -9.0100140477088098e+02. Note run 3 of the racing build:
# -9.0093934416427931e+02, which is wrong in the fifth significant digit rather than obviously
# absurd. A tolerance-based comparison against a reference would have accepted it.
#
# WHY NO EXISTING CHECK CAUGHT IT: the fork's thread-invariance harness compares 1 thread against
# N. Here BOTH sides move, so the comparison is between two wrong answers and can pass. The check
# that catches it is repetition at ONE thread count, which is now in CI and in INSTALL.md.
